From e2863f2ee82b81495ebc079d009ed5f4b70e0cd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 09:27:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07184/11362] [outer-loop] Widen reflect-nudge token budget +
 extend SGE smoke test to 3 games

Two additions on top of REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-3 (reflect() anti-stagnation
prompt nudge):

1. LLMStrategyProposer.reflect_nudge_max_tokens (default 160, vs the
   base 96) gives the completion call more output-token room
   specifically on the nudge-fired path, testing whether the prior
   real-GPU run's reflect-parse failure was a token-budget artifact.

2. scripts/outer_loop_sge_smoke_test.py generalized from a single
   hardcoded g50t run to a 3-game suite (g50t unchanged + sk48,
   already flagged in known-issues.md as a richer-candidate target +
   cd82, a third independent data point), each using that game's own
   precedented shallow-frontier levels from
   ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml. g50t's output path is unchanged for
   backward compat with the existing REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-3 baselines.

Real run (all 3 games, live gemma-4-12B-it, CUDA-pinned): 0/3 leveled
up (g50t stayed L2, sk48 stayed L1, cd82 stayed L1 -- all honest
nulls). More informative than the headline null: the soft
reflect-prompt nudge never got a chance to fire in ANY of the 3 games
this run, because 2 of 3 (g50t, sk48) instead hit the HARD
deterministic collapse override first, which bypasses reflect()
entirely once triggered -- so the token-budget fix remains untested,
and there's a real architectural question (checked in
ops/known-issues.md task 6) about whether the soft nudge needs to be
evaluated more frequently than every reflect_every=6 boundary to ever
get a turn before collapse pre-empts it.

2 new unit tests for reflect_nudge_max_tokens (fires vs default path).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
